# Volla Phone Plinius: input devices for the session only where one of its own services reads them.
# The user plinius was in the group "input": every program of the session, also one an attacker
# got onto the phone outside Flatpak, could read every touch, key and pen stroke, the PIN typed at
# the lock screen included (attack review 2026-11-12, H3). Without the group, phoc gets its devices
# from logind (TakeDevice) as before, and only these two get an ACL for the active user (uaccess):
#   gpio-keys                    plinius-assist (long press of a key)
#   mt6878-mt6369 Headset Jack   audio-hal-bridge (headset plugged in, its buttons)
# The haptics device has its rule in feedbackd (72-feedbackd.rules).
ACTION=="remove", GOTO="plinius_input_session_end"
SUBSYSTEM=="input", KERNEL=="event*", ATTRS{name}=="gpio-keys", TAG+="uaccess"
SUBSYSTEM=="input", KERNEL=="event*", ATTRS{name}=="mt6878-mt6369 Headset Jack", TAG+="uaccess"
LABEL="plinius_input_session_end"
